course: dictionary
lesson: 16189
title: Words for the science of animals
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words name a science. Zoology is the science that studies animals: their bodies, how they live, grow and behave, and where they come from. «Zoology helped our class sort the animals we found in the garden.» The ending -ology often means the study of something, so biology is the study of living things and botany is the study of plants.
explain: A person who works in zoology is a zoologist. A zoologist might work in a lab, at a zoo or out in the wild, watching animals. «My aunt is a zoologist, and she spends her summers counting birds on the coast.» Zoology is uncountable, so we never say «zoologies».
explain: Zoology can also mean the animal life of a place. This is a formal meaning, and you will often find it in books about nature. «The zoology of Australia includes kangaroos, koalas and platypuses.» Here it means all the animals that live in Australia. The clues around the word tell you which meaning fits.
fact: Zoology is one branch of biology.
fact: Botany is the study of plants, and zoology is the study of animals.
fact: Zoologists sort animals into groups such as mammals, birds, reptiles, amphibians, fish and insects.
fact: «Zoology» can also mean the animal life of a place, as in «the zoology of Australia».
fact: Just So Stories tell made-up reasons for animal features, but zoology finds the true reasons, such as how leopards came to have spots through evolution.
exercise: «Zoology helped our class sort the animals we found in the garden.» What does zoology mean here? | *The study of animals | The study of rocks and weather | A type of garden tool | The study of plants
exercise: «The zoology of Australia includes kangaroos, koalas and platypuses.» What does zoology mean in this sentence? | A map of the country | Plants that grow in the desert | *The animal life of a place | A zoo in Sydney
exercise: Which word names a person who studies animals? | botanist | zoology | *zoologist
test: «Mia wants to be a zoologist when she grows up, because she loves studying how animals live.» What is zoology? | *The science that studies animals | The science that studies stars | The study of old buildings
test: Which of these is a group of animals that zoologists sort into? | Vegetables | Minerals | *Amphibians
exam: Which sentence about zoology is correct? | *«Zoology is the study of animals.» | «Zoology is a type of cloud.» | «Zoology is the study of plants.»
